Squaring Eq.  and solving for the angular velocity gives $\dot\theta^{\,2}
=
\frac{\lambda^{2}F}
{r^{2}\left(r^{2}+\lambda^{2}\right)}.$ Substitution into Eq.  leaves an energy that depends only on the proposed radius and the fixed angular momentum: $E(r,\lambda)
=m\sqrt{F(r)}\,\frac{\sqrt{r^{2}+\lambda^{2}}}{r}.$

